+# ---------- transcribed-run verification (agents-m6fr) ----------
+# fleet_verdict_transcribed_run_status <run-id> <named-reviewer-model> [run-root]
+#
+# WHY THIS EXISTS: a verdict posted by the branch author's OWN lane cannot be told from a reviewer
+# subagent's by its actor - reviewer subagents inherit the parent lane's actor (fleet-15b5) - so
+# fleet-ry7m accepts such a verdict on the strength of a NAMED reviewer model of another family.
+# That is a claim written on the comment, not evidence. The foza convention already requires a
+# transcribed verdict to name its source; the run id IS the source, and it is checkable, because
+# subagent run directories are retained on disk with a recovery-descriptor.json naming agent+model.
+#
+# Prints "verified: ..." when the run resolves to a reviewer run whose FAMILY matches the named
+# reviewer model, "unverified: <reason>" otherwise, and nothing at all when there is no run id.
+# Family, not exact string: the recorded model carries a thinking suffix (":high") that the named
+# one does not, and fleet_verdict_model_family is the fleet's existing comparison.
+#
+# LIMIT, STATED RATHER THAN HIDDEN: this proves the run exists and is a reviewer run of the right
+# family. It does NOT prove that run reviewed THIS diff - the descriptor records agent and model,
+# not the bead or the branch. A lane willing to point at an unrelated reviewer run would pass. That
+# is a smaller hole than an unbacked model string, and it is the hole that remains.
+fleet_verdict_transcribed_run_status() {
